msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/features/companion.md:1 docs/features/companion.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Desktop Companion"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Dynamic SAP satellite**: a standalone desktop GUI app, not managed via `config.yaml`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:10
msgid ""
"The desktop companion is a SAP **Type B** app (embedded sidecar holds the "
"Hub WebSocket, `relay: false`): the **content pack** (React + VRM + Node "
"sidecar) is embedded by the **desktop shell** (`src/app/shell/desktop`), "
"registers with the Hub via SAP, and exposes local tools to the Agent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/features/companion.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FreeAnima Desktop (src/app/shell/desktop)\n"
"├── Electron Main — tray / multi-window + embedded companion sidecar\n"
"│   ├── companion overlay — transparent always-on-top, VRM / speech bubble\n"
"│   ├── companion settings — settings window (Hub RPC + asset HTTP)\n"
"│   ├── chat — Chat SPA (SAP direct, no sidecar)\n"
"│   └── console — Console WebView (Hub REST)\n"
"└── Renderer — preload satelliteShell; companion visibility via IPC\n"
"         ↕ SAP WS + Hub RPC\n"
"    anima service Hub (companion_profile SSOT + assets + FBX→VRMA)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/companion.md:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hub vs local boundary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer            | Location                             | Responsibility                                                                                                                                                           |\n"
"| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| **Hub SSOT**     | `src/features/companion/`            | `companion_profile` entity (behavior, slots, library meta); VRM/VRMA files under `~/.anima/companion/` on Hub host; FBX→VRMA conversion; Settings read/write via Hub RPC |\n"
"| **Settings UI**  | Desktop Settings → Companion section | Hub RPC (`companion.config.*`, model/motion CRUD); upload via `POST /hub/rpc/v1/companion/model/upload` and `/companion/motion/import`                                   |\n"
"| **Thin sidecar** | `src/satellites/companion/server/`   | SAP attach, `bubble` / `play_slot`, runtime WebSocket, local asset cache; startup `companion.sync.pull`                                                                  |\n"
"| **Electron**     | `src/app/shell/desktop/`             | Transparent window, click-through, tray, companion show/hide IPC                                                                                                         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:35
msgid ""
"Management is in **Settings only** — Console has no companion admin page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:37
msgid ""
"On sidecar start: Hub config wins; `~/.anima/companion/config.json` on the "
"desktop is an **offline cache**. Legacy local data is migrated once to Hub "
"(`companion.migrate.fromLocal` or HTTP upload). Multiple desktops share the "
"same model/motion library via Hub."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/features/companion.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Settings ──Hub RPC/HTTP──► features/companion (Hub)\n"
"Sidecar  ◄──sync.pull────► Hub          ──► local cache (VRM/VRMA)\n"
"Overlay  ◄──localhost────► Sidecar       (runtime WS + /api/config)\n"
"Electron ◄──IPC──────────► Settings       (show/hide only)\n"
"Agent    ──SAP───────────► Sidecar        (bubble, play_slot)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:47
msgid ""
"The content pack lives in [`src/satellites/companion/`](../../src/satellites/"
"companion/) (`spa/` + thin `server/` + `shared/`). Hub domain logic: [`src/"
"features/companion/`](../../src/features/companion/). Export conventions: "
"[`frontend-exports.md`](../sap/frontend-exports.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:49
msgid "Compared with Chat / pair programming:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|             | Chat / pair programming              | Companion                                            |\n"
"| ----------- | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| UI          | Browser Web UI                       | Native transparent companion window + settings       |\n"
"| Deployment  | Managed (can co-locate with service) | Dynamic (user starts manually)                       |\n"
"| SAP         | Type A or Type B + relay             | Type B + tools, no relay                             |\n"
"| Client & UI | Can be separated                     | Companion render and settings share one Electron app |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <messages><msg>
#: docs/features/companion.md:57 messages/po4a/en.xml:603
#, no-wrap
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"VRM avatar rendering (Three.js + `@pixiv/three-vrm`); VRM 1.0 and 0.x auto "
"orientation correction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"**Motion slots**: five slots — `idle`, `rest`, `walk`, `climb`, `in_place`; "
"each slot binds 0..n VRMA clips; play by id or random; empty slot = no "
"animation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"**Speech bubble**: one-way text queue; user click advances; no auto-dismiss; "
"pushed by Hub Agent via `companion.bubble` tool"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"Transparent always-on-top companion window (160×260); avatar area clickable, "
"empty area click-through"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"**Local interaction**: drag to move window; click body to play random motion "
"from `in_place` slot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"**Patrol** (Settings → Behavior tab): idle patrol, double-click patrol, "
"corner pause, patrol speed, return-to-start on launch, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"System tray: show/hide companion, **Settings…** (open settings window), quit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/features/companion.md:67
msgid ""
"Settings tabs: **General** / **Behavior** / **Models** / **Motion slots** / "
"**Motion library**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/features/companion.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "Agent tools (sidecar registration)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:74
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Tool        | Parameters                           | Description                            |\n"
"| ----------- | ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `bubble`    | `text: string`                       | Enqueue text in speech bubble          |\n"
"| `play_slot` | `slot: string`; `motion_id?: string` | Play motion slot; `motion_id` optional |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:76
msgid ""
"Periodic content (e.g. scheduled jokes) is configured on **anima service / "
"scheduled tasks**; the Agent calls `bubble`. Companion has no built-in timer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/features/companion.md:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "Models and motions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:80
msgid ""
"The repo **does not bundle** `.vrm` / `.vrma` files. **Hub** is the SSOT: "
"`companion_profile` entity in PostgreSQL plus files on the Hub host at "
"`~/.anima/companion/models/` and `motions/`. Each desktop keeps a **local "
"cache** synced on sidecar start (`companion.sync.pull`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/companion.md:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "VRM models"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:84
msgid ""
"Settings → **Models** tab: list, import, delete, rename, switch current "
"model. Upload goes to Hub (`POST /hub/rpc/v1/companion/model/upload`); "
"sidecar downloads missing files for overlay rendering."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:86
msgid ""
"During development, files in `src/satellites/companion/public/models/` serve "
"as fallback."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/companion.md:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "VRMA library and slots"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:90
msgid ""
"Settings → **Motion library** tab: import VRMA, FBX, or ZIP (FBX is "
"converted on **Hub**, not on desktop). **Motion slots** tab assigns motions "
"per slot. Preview supports mouse drag to rotate view."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:92
msgid ""
"Unbound slots play no animation; patrol still moves the window; walk/climb "
"VRMA play only when bound."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/companion.md:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "FBX import"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:96
msgid ""
"FBX→VRMA runs on the **Hub host** (`anima service`). Desktop installers no "
"longer bundle `fbx2vrma-converter` or FBX2glTF. On the Hub machine run `bun "
"run setup:fbx` if FBX conversion is needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/features/companion.md:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "Development and run"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/companion.md:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "Browser dev (no Electron)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/companion.md:102
msgid "In `src/satellites/companion`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/features/companion.md:103
